// THE ONLY IMPURE MODULE IN THE LIBRARY — the PLACEHOLDER (0.0.1 P-7, P-11).
//
// EMPTY ON PURPOSE: see `../core/core.npk` for why a placeholder exists at all.
// It is REPLACED at the cycle below, never deleted. The rule below is carried
// from day one, deliberately: it is what a reader meets before a check
// enforces it.
//
// ============================ THE PURITY RULE ============================
// NO SYSCALL, NO CLOCK, NO ENVIRONMENT READ AND NO FILE READ EXISTS ANYWHERE
// IN THIS LIBRARY EXCEPT IN THIS DIRECTORY (TM-018, `SAFETY.md` §3).
//
// Everything outside `src/host/` is a pure function of its arguments. That is
// what makes the library reproducible, testable with no double, and portable
// by rewriting one module. `check_purity` fails the build when it stops being
// true, and it is the single most important check in the suite.
//
// AND THE ARROW POINTS ONE WAY: NOTHING imports `host` except `src/lib.npk`
// and an application (`BUILD.md` B-17). That is the purity boundary expressed
// as a layering rule, and `check_layering` enforces it.
// =========================================================================
//
// WHAT FILLS IT: five functions and nothing else — `host_now_utc`,
// `host_now_instant`, `host_now_boot`, `host_clock_res`, `host_system_zone` —
// with `clock_gettime` reached through `sys` and a 16-byte `timespec` laid out
// in a `buffer` (probe 03 pinned that shape). Governed by
// `meta/specs/HOST.md`.
// WHEN: cycle 0.3 (`meta/roadmap/0.3/README.md`), which is also when
// `check_purity` goes live and must be SEEN TO FAIL against a planted
// `mono_now()` outside this directory.
//
// WHAT IT MAY IMPORT: `zone` (for the name lookup), `cal` (for the range
// check) and `core` (`BUILD.md` B-17).
//
// THE ERRORS IT RAISES: none of its own — kernel errnos are FORWARDED VERBATIM
// (`SAFETY.md` S-5), exactly as `lib/nsys.npk` does.
mod:host;
